Problem Statement 19
Weightage: 1
Status: Unattempted
A junior data engineer has ingested a JSON file into a table raw_table with the following schema: cart_id STRING, items ARRAY The junior data engineer would like to unnest the items column in raw_table to result in a new table with the following schema: cart_id STRING, item_id STRING Which of the following commands should the junior data engineer run to complete this task?
1. SELECT cart_id, filter(items) AS item_id FROM raw_table;
2. SELECT cart_id, flatten(items) AS item_id FROM raw_table;
3. SELECT cart_id, reduce(items) AS item_id FROM raw_table;
4. SELECT cart_id, explode(items) AS item_id FROM raw_table;
5. SELECT cart_id, slice(items) AS item_id FROM raw_table;
